In order to work in Ireland a non-EEA National, unless they are exempted, must hold a valid employment permit.  Please review the Eligibility and requirements for an employment permit if you are unsure of your eligibility to apply for this vacancy. <br>  Job Title: Car Mechanic 
Company Name: Northside Tyre Depot
Job Location: Unit 2a, Eklad Park, Malahide Road Industrial Park, Dublin 17, D17 CD43

We are looking for a Car Mechanic to join our team, responsible for carrying out inspections, repairs and maintenance on motor vehicles, ensuring safety, quality and efficiency in the services provided.

Responsibilities
-Visually checks, test drives or uses test equipment to diagnose engine and mechanical faults;
-Removes, dismantles, repairs and replaces defective parts and prepares new parts using appropriate tools;
-Reassembles, tests, adjusts and tunes the appropriate parts, systems or entire engine;
-Carries out routine maintenance checks on oil and air filters, brakes and other vehicle parts/systems;
-Diagnoses faults in electrical/electronic circuitry, removes faulty components and fits replacements;
-Checks condition of electrical/electronic systems and carries out servicing tasks;
-Repairs and services air conditioning, heating and engine-cooling systems.

Requirements
-No formal academic qualification required;
-Previous experience in automotive mechanics will be considered an advantage;
-Ability to work in a team and strong attention to detail;
-Willingness to learn and continuously improve.

Annual Salary: €36.605
Hours Salary: €18.05
 Weekly Hours: 39 hours
Start Date: 12.10.26
Company Contact:
Michael Hanley
Email: northsidetyredepot@hotmail.com

